                    {
                        "form_id": "0c199bf9-4a1c-4523-8fe9-9ab0f0eaa296",
                        "entry_id": "e7fcd828-728e-3044-bbaf-799eb44251d5",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "assoiled"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dc1f6a9a-87c9-3c2e-803a-12b478cd615e",
                        "entry_id": "e7fcd828-728e-3044-bbaf-799eb44251d5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To absolve or release (someone) from blame or sin; to forgive, to pardon."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d32212dd-cf43-484c-96e2-5dad1a23243d",
                                "sense_id": "dc1f6a9a-87c9-3c2e-803a-12b478cd615e",
                                "text": "But ſecretly aſſoyling of his ſin, / No other med'cine vvill he to him lay, / Saying that Heauen his ſiluer him ſhould vvin, / And to giue Friers, vvas better then to pray, / So he vvere ſhrieu'd, vvhat need he care a pin?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "30c82152-13b6-4724-bd79-eb3753bdf90e",
                                "sense_id": "dc1f6a9a-87c9-3c2e-803a-12b478cd615e",
                                "text": "Pray deuoutly for the ſoule whom God aſſoile of one of the moſt worſhipfull Knights in his daies of manhood and cunning, Richard Beauchampe late Earle of Warwicke, […] [Inscription on the deceased's tomb.]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "53f3edda-f6b4-4ff3-b9a1-403ce20f1ecc",
                                "sense_id": "dc1f6a9a-87c9-3c2e-803a-12b478cd615e",
                                "text": "Lord thou ne taughteſt not thy diſciples to aſſoilen men of their ſinne, and ſetten them a penance for their ſinne, in faſting ne in praying, ne other almous deed: […] For Lord, thou forgeue men her ſinnes, and bede him ſinne no more. […] And Lord, thou ne aſſoildeſt no man both of his ſinne and of his peine, that vvas due for his ſinne, ne thou grantedſt no man ſuch povver heere on earth."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "441e1fc6-e2ef-4211-b6fb-75fd2c748cd9",
                                "sense_id": "dc1f6a9a-87c9-3c2e-803a-12b478cd615e",
                                "text": "[M]any persons think themselves fairly assoiled, because they are no adulterers, no rebels, no drunkards, not of scandalous lives; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5fa21fa4-d2ce-49ad-bf73-ce482c84ebdb",
                                "sense_id": "dc1f6a9a-87c9-3c2e-803a-12b478cd615e",
                                "text": "[B]eing juſtified by Faith, in a Forenſal ſenſe, that is, acquitted and aſſoiled from the guilt of all our ſins, as vvell as in ſeveral meaſures, according to our ſeveral ages and grovvths in Chriſtianity; […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dbe4a85a-06e8-3deb-8364-bacd3e41a900",
                        "entry_id": "e7fcd828-728e-3044-bbaf-799eb44251d5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To atone or expiate for (something)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e76cb355-7941-40d7-97e4-a80693128422",
                                "sense_id": "dbe4a85a-06e8-3deb-8364-bacd3e41a900",
                                "text": "But Glauce, ſeeing all that chaunced there, / VVell vveeting hovv their errour to aſſoyle, / Full glad of ſo good end, to them drevv nere, / And her ſalevved vvith ſeemly belaccoyle, / Ioyous to ſee her ſafe after long toyle."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f6989256-66e3-4b54-84e6-9c503b51a36a",
                                "sense_id": "dbe4a85a-06e8-3deb-8364-bacd3e41a900",
                                "text": "And theſe reaſons verily induce me to beleeve, that in times paſt they choſe the Bay tree for their triumphs, before any other: rather than as Maſſurius vvould have it, becauſe the Lavvrell ſerved for a ſolemne perfume, to expiate and aſſoile the carnage and execution done upon the enemies."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "44c7e53f-122f-4868-bca8-0d2e91fbd374",
                                "sense_id": "dbe4a85a-06e8-3deb-8364-bacd3e41a900",
                                "text": "Let each act / Assoil a fault or help a merit grow: / Like threads of silver seen through crystal beads / Let love through good deeds show."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e44acb6a-c2d6-3d57-9036-bfca553cc16f",
                        "entry_id": "e7fcd828-728e-3044-bbaf-799eb44251d5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Followed by from or of: to acquit (someone) from a criminal charge; to find (someone) not guilty; to clear."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8e91e68c-5752-497b-a0c9-0671b57574ae",
                                "sense_id": "e44acb6a-c2d6-3d57-9036-bfca553cc16f",
                                "text": "For if the mater appere vpon his ſyde therby, either clere or doubtefull, than may the iudges acquite and aſſoyle the defendaũt [defendaunt]. And better were it the faute to be quytte, than the fautles to be punyſhed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eb1aa17c-e050-4ace-a960-38b8d7a00ecb",
                                "sense_id": "e44acb6a-c2d6-3d57-9036-bfca553cc16f",
                                "text": "Whom Ceſar doth condemne, god ſumtime doeth aſſoyle: and whom the prince doth aſſoyle, he leaueth in the cumpany of mẽ [men], to make other like himſelf: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "278f5780-ecb6-4e43-8d71-5784ba7701d3",
                                "sense_id": "e44acb6a-c2d6-3d57-9036-bfca553cc16f",
                                "text": "Then are there 70 judges deputed to ſit upon his cauſe; and if it happen that they aſſoile and quit this partie condemned: then thoſe 30 vvho condemned him, are diſplaced from their ſtate and dignitie, vvith a moſt bitter and greevous rebuke, and for ever after, as diſgraced perſons live in ſhame and infamie."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "00dbbe9c-45c2-3b31-8b12-5e544cbc379a",
                        "entry_id": "e7fcd828-728e-3044-bbaf-799eb44251d5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Followed by from or of: to release or set free (someone) from a liability, an obligation, etc.; to discharge."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "obsolete",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3607126c-917f-465e-b2e3-0a52daf5a4ee",
                                "sense_id": "00dbbe9c-45c2-3b31-8b12-5e544cbc379a",
                                "text": "But firſt thou muſt a ſeaſon faſt and pray, / Till from her bands the ſpright aſſoiled is, / And haue her ſtrength recur'd from fraile infirmitis."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0b304d8c-2ae7-4147-af6e-f1ac5a3808b2",
                                "sense_id": "00dbbe9c-45c2-3b31-8b12-5e544cbc379a",
                                "text": "His vvearie ghoſt aſſoyld from fleſhly band, / Did not as others vvont, directly fly / Vnto her reſt in Plutoes grieſly land, / Ne into ayre did vaniſh preſently, / Ne chaunged vvas into a ſtarre in sky: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b23bc2b-f87d-414a-953c-ba8be8b79a31",
                                "sense_id": "00dbbe9c-45c2-3b31-8b12-5e544cbc379a",
                                "text": "What are we set on earth for? Say, to toil— / Nor seek to leave thy tending of the vines, / For all the heat o' the day, till it declines, / And Death's mild curfew shall from work assoil."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0e5ce9f3-53c8-300e-9a36-598c2734f0ab",
                        "entry_id": "e7fcd828-728e-3044-bbaf-799eb44251d5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To clear up or resolve (a difficulty, doubt, problem, etc.); to absolve, to solve."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "78c9c204-5a02-4a1d-ba41-8849db456c96",
                                "sense_id": "0e5ce9f3-53c8-300e-9a36-598c2734f0ab",
                                "text": "I ſaie, aſſoyleth this doubt and queſtion, by the only argument and aſſuraunce of the knovven Catholik church of Chriſt."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "183ead9c-7451-4a87-b4c4-eba27bea5b4c",
                                "sense_id": "0e5ce9f3-53c8-300e-9a36-598c2734f0ab",
                                "text": "Here M. [Thomas] Harding once againe moueth a very néedeleſſe queſtion. VVe demaunde, ſaithe he, vvhether vvee receiue the ſame Body of Chriſte by Faithe onely, vvithout our Body, or vvith the office of our Body. Any childe might ſoone be hable to aſſoile this reddle."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "403a2d81-a373-4013-9f1e-780510ef118d",
                                "sense_id": "0e5ce9f3-53c8-300e-9a36-598c2734f0ab",
                                "text": "[O]thers, held very good men, are at a dead ſtand, not knovving vvhat to doe or ſay; and are therefore called Seekers, looking for nevv Nuntio's from Chriſt, to aſſoil theſe benighted queſtions, and to give nevv Orders for nevv Churches."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "05389bd4-3022-34d1-a30c-40917a4bc7be",
                        "entry_id": "e7fcd828-728e-3044-bbaf-799eb44251d5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To refute (an argument, an objection, etc.)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8d974ccc-f21a-373d-bd6e-745eab374120",
                        "entry_id": "e7fcd828-728e-3044-bbaf-799eb44251d5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To discharge (a liability, an obligation, etc.)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete",
                            "rare",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fe1d3be3-fa21-441f-acff-57f46581b6f1",
                                "sense_id": "8d974ccc-f21a-373d-bd6e-745eab374120",
                                "text": "And ye poore Pilgrimes, that vvith reſtleſſe toyle / VVearie your ſelues in vvandring deſert vvayes, / Till that you come, vvhere ye your vovves aſſoyle, / VVhen paſsing by ye read theſe vvofull layes / On my graue vvritten, […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4dc998f2-7f12-3ddb-8eea-8dbac65c6178",
                        "entry_id": "e7fcd828-728e-3044-bbaf-799eb44251d5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To get rid of, put off, or remove (something)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete",
                            "rare",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0a847c30-2029-4ab4-a27e-077b2e2ea277",
                                "sense_id": "4dc998f2-7f12-3ddb-8eea-8dbac65c6178",
                                "text": "She ſoundly ſlept, & carefull thoughts did quite aſſoile."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "687a0cf3-990c-3b57-8433-eb7062c974c7",
                        "entry_id": "e7fcd828-728e-3044-bbaf-799eb44251d5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To absolve or release (someone) from excommunication or some other religious offence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "11f665cb-f864-4f11-a78b-8a29baf5dd54",
                                "sense_id": "687a0cf3-990c-3b57-8433-eb7062c974c7",
                                "text": "[H]is Barons […] flatly oppoſe themſelues both to his commaund and their Countries good, denying him (vntill he vvere aſſoyled of his excommunication,) their attendance in ſo behouefull a ſeruice."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
